at this level range. Quest and crafted pieces are listed in the sections below.",keys={"shaman-g452","shaman-g530","shaman-g22","shaman-g492","shaman-g38","shaman-g443","shaman-g482","shaman-g469","shaman-g453","shaman-g525","shaman-g522","shaman-g149","shaman-g427","shaman-g507","shaman-g83"}},{b="30-39",no="Best match per slot for Restoration by stat priority, picked from dungeon drops, quest rewards and crafting at this level range. Quest and crafted pieces are listed in the sections below.",keys={"shaman-g659","shaman-g633","shaman-g645","shaman-g577","shaman-g664","shaman-g588","shaman-g582","shaman-g558","shaman-g650","shaman-g551","shaman-g640","shaman-g668","shaman-g618","shaman-g581"}},{b="40-49",no="Best match per slot for Restoration by stat priority, picked from dungeon drops, quest rewards and crafting at this level range. Quest and crafted pieces are listed in the sections below.",keys={"shaman-g67","shaman-g831","shaman-g808","shaman-g787","shaman-g697","shaman-g744","shaman-g772","shaman-g774","shaman-g732","shaman-g779","shaman-g680","shaman-g75","shaman-g790","shaman-g728","shaman-g821","shaman-g709"}},{b="50-60",no="Best match per slot for Restoration by stat priority, picked from dungeon drops, quest rewards and crafting at this level range. Quest and crafted pieces are listed in the sections below.",keys={"shaman-g969","shaman-g991","shaman-g975","shaman-g1011","shaman-g981","shaman-g970","shaman-g1014","shaman-g1068","shaman-g979","shaman-g886","shaman-g84","shaman-g12","shaman-g912","shaman-g920","shaman-g1053","shaman-g42","shaman-g1036"}}},title="Restoration | WoW Forever Shaman Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[767]},{id="journey",x=S[560]},{id="talents",x=S[484]},{id="stats",x=S[608]},{id="combat",x=S[609]},{id="macros",x=S[610]},{id="dungeons",x=S[540]},{id="professions",x=S[561]},{id="crafting",x=S[549]},{id="questgear",x=S[531]},{id=S[483],x=S[702]}},asideNote=S[68],talentString="00000000000000000550000000000000005530003315513151",ranks={{tree="Enhancement",name=S[611],r=5,max=5},{tree="Enhancement",name=S[593],r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Improved Healing Wave",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Tidal Focus",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Mindfulness",r=3,max=3},{tree="Restoration",name="Ancestral Healing",r=3,max=3},{tree="Restoration",name="Healing Focus",r=3,max=3},{tree="Restoration",name=S[819],r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name="Tidal Mastery",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Restorative Totems",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name=S[707],r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name="Healing Way",r=3,max=3},{tree="Restoration",name="Nature's Swiftness",r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name="Purification",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Riptide",r=1,max=1}},order={},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[532]},{t="h1",x="Restoration",sub=S[612]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Keep the party stable with efficient single-target heals, Riptide and well-aimed Chain Heals, supported by Water Shield, Mana Tide and encounter-specific totems."},{t="pills",list={S[699],S[562]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[768]},{t="h2",x=S[452]},{t="p",x=S[66]},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Learn healing judgment"},{t="p",x="For a group-focused route, begin with Restoration healing and efficiency talents. Heal missing health rather than casting continuously at full-health targets. Outside a group, use trained Lightning Bolt and melee carefully; this healing endpoint is not a promise of fast solo damage."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Build reliable recovery"},{t="p",x="Develop Water Shield, casting protection and mana support as their talent gates open. Use Healing Wave when time allows and Lesser Healing Wave for faster responses. Learn the poison and disease tools available at your level. Keep line of sight to the tank and drink before the next pull."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Add group healing depth"},{t="p",x="Chain Heal becomes available at 40; obtain Riptide through your chosen talents and combine them when group damage justifies it. Finish the Restoration investment, then the selected ten Enhancement points for critical chance and Intellect. Keep a damage set for solo errands if useful."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[485]},{t="h2",x=S[699]},{t="p",x="Tree order: Elemental / Enhancement / Restoration. These 51 points and selected ranks were checked against your supplied Standards.gg build. The link below is preloaded; changes made inside the calculator do not automatically rewrite this guide."},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[541]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="p",s="notice",x="This 0/10/41 allocation includes the main Restoration actives and full Healing Focus. It spends no points on Natural Grace, Totemic Focus or Improved Reincarnation. Plan threat, totem mana costs and recovery around those omissions."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[613]},{t="h2",x=S[509]},{t="p",x="Restoration wants healing power first, then the mana stats that keep you casting. Critical strike adds burst healing."},{t="h3",x=S[734]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[912],x="or spell power"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Intellect",x=S[793]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spirit",x=S[588]},{t="stat",i=4,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Mana per 5",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="When you quest alone, spell damage and Intellect also speed up kills. Keep a healing set for dungeons."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[912],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b=S[703],x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spirit",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Mana per 5",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Healers do not need hit for heals. Balance healing power against mana stats depending on how long fights last."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Mana per 5 keeps working while you cast; Spirit regeneration stops for 5 seconds after each spell that costs mana. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[510]},{t="h2",x=S[550]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="h4",x="Prepare Water Shield and positioning"},{t="p",x="Maintain Water Shield once learned, checking its charges during recovery windows. It shares the elemental-shield slot with Lightning Shield. Stand where you can see the tank and reach likely damage targets, while avoiding cleaves and unnecessary movement."},{t="h4",x="Choose a heal that lands in time"},{t="p",x="Use Healing Wave for a suitable cast window and Lesser Healing Wave when a faster heal is necessary. Match the heal to expected damage and missing health; overhealing wastes mana. Rank choice should follow the current tooltip, cost and outcome rather than a blanket lowest-rank rule."},{t="h4",x="Keep Riptide rolling"},{t="p",x="Riptide is a cheap heal over time with no up-front healing, on a 12-second cooldown. Cast it on cooldown on the most injured ally, ideally the target you will Chain Heal next, because Chain Heal heals a Riptide target for 25% more. For immediate healing, use Healing Wave, or Nature’s Swiftness in an emergency."},{t="h4",x="Aim Chain Heal at an injured cluster"},{t="p",x="Start on an appropriate injured target with nearby allies who also need healing. A spread group may get more value from individual heals. Check actual bounce positioning rather than assuming three useful targets. Avoid spending Chain Heal mana just to fill a small amount of missing health."},{t="h4",x="Time emergency tools and mana support"},{t="p",x="Use Nature’s Swiftness with a suitable Nature heal when a normal cast will be too late. Use Mana Tide while its recovery can be useful to the party and before you have no options left. Coordinate totems, cleanse harmful poison or disease, and communicate when the group must pause."},{t="abil",names={"Healing Wave","Lesser Healing Wave","Riptide","Chain Heal",S[819],S[707]}},{t="h3",x=S[646]},{t="p",x="Compare healing power, Intellect, useful mana regeneration and enough Stamina for the encounter. Spell-damage-only gear is not healing gear. Cloth or leather can be reasonable alternatives to mail when their healing stats are stronger, but assess the defensive loss. Weapon damage does not improve heals."},{t="p",x=S[64]},{t="h3",x=S[504]},{t="p",x=S[56]},{t="p",x=S[52]},{t="p",x=S[124]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[614]},{t="h2",x=S[424]},{t="p",x=S[59]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[40]},{t="macro",n=S[551],x=S[126],code=S[201]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[120],code=S[175]},{t="macro",n=S[594],x=S[113],code=S[199]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[122],code=S[266]},{t="macro",n=S[563],x=S[121],code=S[230]},{t="macro",n=S[564],x=S[155],code=S[207]},{t="macro",n=S[552],x=S[247],code=S[202]},{t="macro",n=S[542],x=S[158],code=S[179]},{t="macro",n=S[565],x=S[94],code=S[173]},{t="macro",n=S[505],x=S[129],code=S[267]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[160],code=S[342]},{t="macro",n=S[469],x=S[115],code=S[225]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Chain Heal",x="Start the chain on the hovered ally, friendly target or yourself. Choose the first recipient and let the normal bounce rules determine later recipients.",code="#showtooltip Chain Heal\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Chain Heal"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Riptide",x="Apply your selected instant heal to a living friendly mouseover, friendly target or yourself. Use only after learning the talent.",code="#showtooltip Riptide\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Riptide"},{t="macro",n="Emergency instant Healing Wave",x="Stops your current cast, activates your selected Nature’s Swiftness, then attempts Healing Wave. It still needs a valid recipient and sufficient mana; if the cooldown is unavailable it can begin a normal cast.",code="#showtooltip Nature's Swiftness\n/stopcasting\n/cast Nature's Swiftness\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Healing Wave"},{t="macro",n="Refresh Water Shield",x="Reapply your selected mana shield when useful. Replaces Lightning Shield because only one elemental shield can be active.",code="#showtooltip Water Shield\n/cast Water Shield"},{t="macro",n=S[707],x="Place your selected mana-recovery totem when the party can benefit. Keep it separate from routine totem presets so you do not spend the cooldown accidentally.",code="#showtooltip Mana Tide Totem\n/cast Mana Tide Totem"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[256]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[705]},{t="h2",x=S[474]},{t="p",x=S[60]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[46]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[74]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[511]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[543]},{t="h2",x=S[453]},{t="p",x=S[37]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[512]},{t="h2",x=S[420]},{t="p",x=S[41]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[483]},{t="kicker",x=S[706]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[91]}}}},dungeons={{n=S[257],lr="13–18",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={},t={},no={S[28]}}},{n=S[169],lr="13–18",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={},t={},no={S[28]}}},{n=S[226],lr="15–24",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={{n=S[725],st=S[112],no=S[36],it={{id=6632,n=S[887]}}}},t={},no={S[28]}}},{n=S[85],lr="15–20",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={{n="Lordaeron Captain",st="Reported Forever rare",no=S[36],it={}}},t={{id=286980,n=S[850],mob=S[29],st=S[119],no=S[45]},{id=286979,n=S[804],mob=S[29],st=S[119],no=S[45]},{id=286978,n=S[851],mob=S[29],st=S[119],no=S[45]}},no={S[28]}}},{n=S[153],lr="17–26",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={{n="Miner Johnson",st=S[112],no=S[36],it={}}},t={{id=1929,n=S[716],mob=S[29],st=S[35],no=S[15]}},no={S[28]}}},{n=S[159],lr="20–30",st=S[127],no=S[13],ba=true,ra={ck=S[205],r={{n="Deathsworn Captain",st=S[112],no=S[36],it={}}},t={{id=2292,n=S[868],mob=S[29],st=S[35],no=S[15]},{id=1974,n=S[801